.TH PATINA-COMPOSITOR 1 "2026-10-18" "patina-desktop 0.1.0" "Patina Desktop"
.SH NAME
patina-compositor \- Wayland compositor of the Patina desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patina-compositor
.RB [ \-\-greeter
.IR COMMAND ]
.RB [ \-\-shell
.IR COMMAND ]...
.RB [ \-\-per\-output
.IR COMMAND ]
.RI [ COMMAND ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patina-compositor
is a Wayland compositor with floating windows.
Window titlebars, shadows and rounded corners are drawn by the compositor, and clients are
asked not to draw their own.
It supports xdg-shell, layer-shell, xdg-decoration, viewporter, cursor-shape,
wlr-foreign-toplevel-management and ext-workspace. There are four workspaces; they are
switched from the panel.
.PP
Each
.I COMMAND
is a shell command started once the compositor is listening, with
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
set to its socket. The
.B \-\-per\-output
command (the panel) is started once for every display as it is connected, with
.B PATINA_OUTPUT
set to the display's name, and stopped when the display is unplugged. Usually this is done by
.BR patina-session (1).
.PP
A
.B \-\-shell
command (the dock) is started again if it stops. With
.B \-\-greeter
the compositor runs only that sign-in screen and ends when it ends (see
.BR patina-greeter (1)).
.PP
When started from a login session on a seat it drives the display through DRM/KMS and reads
input with libinput. When
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
or
.B DISPLAY
is set it runs inside that session as a window.
.PP
Every connected display on every GPU is used, placed side by side from left to right in the
order they were found, at its preferred resolution. Displays and GPUs can be plugged in and
unplugged while the session runs. Windows on a display that is unplugged move to the first
display. Display-only adapters (USB and DisplayLink docks, for example) work, but their
frames are copied through memory and drawn in software, which costs CPU time.
.SH INPUT
The keyboard layout is the system's: the one in
.I /etc/default/keyboard
or set with
.BR localectl (1).
The
.B XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT
family of variables overrides it. Keys repeat after 400 ms. A touchscreen works on the built-in
display (or the first one): touches go to applications, and a touch on a window frame moves,
resizes or presses its buttons.
.SH LOCKING AND IDLE
Ctrl+Alt+L locks the screen with
.BR patina-lock (1),
as does
.B loginctl lock-session
and going to sleep. After a minute without input the screen dims (the backlight goes down to
30%, or the picture darkens where there is no backlight); after 15 minutes the screen locks
and the computer sleeps. Programs that play video can hold this off (the idle-inhibit
protocol).
.SH MOUSE AND KEYBOARD
.TP
Drag the titlebar
Move the window.
.TP
Double-click the titlebar
Maximise or restore the window.
.TP
Drag the bottom-right corner
Resize the window.
.TP
Titlebar buttons
Minimise, maximise or restore, and close.
.TP
Alt+M
Bring back the most recently minimised window. This is temporary, until the dock exists.
.TP
Super+1 to Super+4
Switch to that workspace. The number-row keys are matched by position, so this works on layouts
where the digits need Shift.
.TP
Super+Shift+1 to Super+Shift+4
Move the focused window to that workspace and switch there.
.TP
Ctrl+Alt+F1 to F12
Switch to another virtual terminal (DRM backend only).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATINA_BACKEND
.BR drm " or " winit .
Overrides the automatic choice of backend.
.TP
.B PATINA_NO_PLANES
When set, everything including the pointer is drawn into one frame instead of using hardware
planes. Needed when capturing the screen from a virtual machine.
.TP
.B PATINA_NO_BLUR
When set, the blur behind the panel and windows is not drawn. Use it on machines where
rendering is slow.
.TP
.B PATINA_IDLE_DIM
Seconds without input before the screen dims (default 60; 0 never).
.TP
.B PATINA_IDLE_SLEEP
Seconds without input before the screen locks and the computer sleeps (default 900; 0 never).
.TP
.B PATINA_LOCKER
Command that locks the screen (default
.BR patina-lock ).
.TP
.B PATINA_SCALE
Display scale, overriding the one chosen from each display's pixel density: one number for all
displays, such as
.BR 1.5 ,
or a list by display name, such as
.BR eDP-1=2,HDMI-A-1=1 .
.TP
.B PATINA_FULL_RECOMPOSE
When set, the whole screen is repainted whenever anything changes, instead of only the changed
areas. A fallback if a repaint ever looks wrong.
.TP
.B PATINA_VERIFY_RECOMPOSE
When set, every frame is also composed in full and compared with the partial one, and
differences are logged. For testing; it roughly doubles the rendering work.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, for example
.BR patina_compositor=debug .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patina-session (1),
.BR patina-panel (1),
.BR patina-lock (1)
